{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2239 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "07a2d5ead14d42dea238f54496dbd8aeac9835bd6836bf7ba2081b11fb7d5b3c" :edb/db-before-t 2238 :edb/db-after-t 2239 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535551 50 #inst "2026-10-09T02:24:39.923Z" 13194139535551 true] [17592186087686 1020 #edb/ref 17592186354876 13194139535551 true] [17592186088090 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535551 true] [17592186088090 1100 "Consider a linear transformation $T$. If $v_{1} + v_{2} = 0$ and $T(v_{1}) = \\begin{bmatrix}54 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 30\\end{bmatrix}$, find $T(21v_{1} + 18v_{2})$." 13194139535551 false] [17592186088090 1100 "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}54 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]\\,$, find $\\,T(21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2}).$" 13194139535551 true] [17592186088090 1145 "First, since ${v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2} & =18{v}_{1}+3{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2} \\\\  & =18({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})+3{v}_{1} \\\\  & =18(0)+3{v}_{1} \\\\  & =3{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nT(21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2})=T(3{v}_{1}).\n$$\n\nNow, since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that $T(kv)=kT(v).$ So \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3{v}_{1}) & =3T({v}_{1}) \\\\  & =3[\\begin{aligned}54 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}162 \\\\ -108 \\\\ 90\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, $T(21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}162 \\\\ -108 \\\\ 90\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535551 true] [17592186088091 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535551 true] [17592186088091 1100 "Consider a linear transformation $T$. If $T(v_{1} + 3v_{2}) = \\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}$ and $T(v_{1}) = \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}$, then find $T(v_{2})$." 13194139535551 false] [17592186088091 1100 "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T({v}_{1}+3{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]$, then find $\\,T({v}_{2}).$" 13194139535551 true] [17592186088091 1145 "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v+kw)=T(v)+T(kw)=T(v)+kT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({v}_{1}+3{v}_{2}) & =T({v}_{1})+3T({v}_{2}) \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]+3T({v}_{2}) \\\\ 3T({v}_{2}) & =[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 3T({v}_{2}) & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535551 true] [17592186088361 1100 "Let\n$T: \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}y \\\\ x\\end{bmatrix}$.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $T(kv) = kT(v)$ for any real $2 \\cdot 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\n2. $T(v_{1} + v_{2}) = T(v_{1}) + T(v_{2})$ for any real $2 \\cdot 1$ column vectors $v_{1}$ and $v_{2}$\n3. $T$ is a linear transformation" 13194139535551 false] [17592186088361 1100 "Let \n$T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}y \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\n- $T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$\n- $T$ is a linear transformation" 13194139535551 true] [17592186354876 1017 #edb/ref 17592186354877 13194139535551 true] [17592186354876 1089 "q-74780" 13194139535551 true] [17592186354876 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535551 true] [17592186354876 1100 "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\,$, find $\\,T(13{v}_{1}+8{v}_{2}).$" 1319413953555